			"Message": "refactor(Wind/Bootstrap): Enhance type safety and Effect-TS integration across service layer\n\nThis commit significantly improves Wind's type safety and architectural alignment with Effect-TS patterns by refactoring service definitions, type imports, and error handling throughout the bootstrap system. The changes reinforce Wind's role as the Effect-TS native service layer in the Land editor architecture.\n\nKey improvements include:\n- Updated Effect-TS service tags to use modern class-based pattern in CoreServices\n- Consolidated type imports from `Types/Types.js` to `Types/BootstrapTypes.ts`\n- Enhanced error handling in Clipboard service with proper Effect error channels\n- Added global TauriInvoke type declaration for better backend communication\n- Fixed Jest configuration structure and added ts-jest for proper TypeScript testing\n- Improved MountainIntegrationService by removing unused performance tracking\n- Enhanced WindInstantiationService with Microsoft-style dependency injection patterns\n\nThese changes strengthen Wind's foundation as it evolves toward the final Effect-TS based architecture, ensuring robust service layer communication with Mountain via Tauri commands and proper error handling across all bootstrap stages.",
			"SHA": "f5f1baf48fa3849e20aadafcbf37672db571839b"
		},
